🇬🇧 The Times reports Russia arming ‘shadow fleet’ tankers

The Times claims Russia has begun installing weapons on some tankers of its so-called “shadow fleet.” In particular, machine guns were allegedly spotted on the gas carrier Marshal Vasilevsky, which could be used not only for defense against drones but also to repel boarding attempts. Experts interviewed by the publication expressed the “unexpected” thought that such actions could seriously complicate future strategies to seize Russian ships in neutral waters. Of course, if all this is actually used. Weapons don’t fire by themselves.

